{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The zeta function is the interference pattern of all prime frequencies simultaneously:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b zeta(s) = product over primes p of 1/(1 - p^(-s))}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The zeros are where all prime frequencies cancel. The critical line is where they cancel symmetrically. Riemann is entropy because it is continuous, increasing, filling \u8212- the thermodynamic arrow applied to the distribution of primes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The primes are not the signal. The primes are the harmonics. They translate the curved Riemannian space onto a flat integer lattice without distorting it. The curvature is preserved in the gaps. The Riemann zeros are the residual curvature that survives the translation \u8212- what the natural log could not flatten.\par}
